     This is a port of the IJG JPEG library to OS-9/68000. The compilation wasdone with GNU gcc2 ver. 2.5.8 and with PD dmake. Very few changes to the codehad to be done. They are marked with "#ifdef OSK" or similarly and mostlyconcern distinguishing between CR and LF.     The libraries are in subdirectory LIB, the executables (cjpeg, djpeg andothers) in CMDS and the original documentation in DOCS. The libraries andexecutables are in two versions: with the ending .070 and without this ending.These with ending .070 have been compiled with the option -m68000 and areappropriate for the 68000, 68010 or 68070 microprocessors and for the 68300series with EC000. These without this ending have been  compiled with theoption -mcpu32 and are good for 68020 or higher and for the  68300 series withCPU32 (like 68340) or CPU32+.     For your convenience, the PostScript translations of the original troffdocumentation are also given.    Andrzej Kotanski    (kotanski@desy.de)                                                       Cracow, March 12, 1995